  "description": "`global name = value` declares a SHARED binding in the root scope (spec/execution-model.md:545-569) — the one variable a procedure can see besides its own parameters and locals, for reading and for writing alike, with no ceremony at the point of assignment. This is the `global` section's own worked example: `bump` says only `:count = :count + 1`, and two calls accumulate to `2`.",
